{{Iron Guide Links}}[[Crafting]] is a skill that Ironmen typically train through [[glassblowing]], due to its low cost and availability. Many pieces of important jewellery require Crafting, such as [[teleportation jewellery]] and [[amulet of glory|amulets of glory]].

==Early training and Quests: 1-35==
{{Main|Quest experience rewards#Crafting}}

Do various quests that give Crafting experience for the early levels. Completing all of these quests will net a total of 23,856 Crafting experience, enough for at least level 35 Crafting. 

* Free-to-play starting quests include:
** [[Sheep Shearer]] rewards 150 Crafting experience
** [[Goblin Diplomacy]] rewards 200 Crafting experience
** [[Misthalin Mystery]] rewards 600 Crafting experience
* [[Dwarf Cannon]] rewards 750 Crafting experience
* [[Recipe for Disaster/Freeing the Goblin generals]] rewards 1,000 Crafting experience (a continuation of Goblin Diplomacy)
* [[Murder Mystery]] rewards 1,406 Crafting experience, which has no requirements and leads to spinning flax.
* [[Observatory Quest]] rewards 2,250 Crafting experience
* [[Death on the Isle]] requires {{SCP|Thieving|34}} and {{SCP|Agility|32}}, rewards 5,000 Crafting experience
* [[Elemental Workshop I]] and [[Elemental Workshop II|II]] will net a total of 12,500 Crafting (and Smithing) experience, with relatively low skill requirements.
** [[Elemental Workshop I]] requires {{SCP|Crafting|20}}, {{SCP|Mining|20}}, {{SCP|Smithing|20}}, rewards 5,000 Crafting experience
** [[Elemental Workshop II]] requires [[Elemental Workshop I]], {{SCP|Magic|20}}, {{SCP|Smithing|30}}, rewards 7,500 Crafting experience

Early alternative training methods and token experience include:

* [[Molten glass]] on [[Entrana]] using the local [[seaweed]] and [[Sandpit|sand]] can provide a source of free Crafting experience for both new and experienced players alike.
* Collecting [[flax]] south of [[Seers' Village]] and [[Spinning Wheel|spinning]] them into [[bow string]]s (requires {{SCP|Crafting|10|link=yes}}) is a good way to gain a few early Crafting levels. Completing [[Murder Mystery]] at {{SCP|Crafting|1|link=yes}}, which is a quest just north of Seers' Village in [[Sinclair Mansion]], will bring the player to {{SCP|Crafting|11|link=yes}}, enough to start spinning flax. Bow strings can be used for [[Fletching]] training and moneymaking from bows.
* Doing [[Bird house trapping|birdhouse]] runs provides small amounts of Crafting experience that add up over time if done regularly.
* [[Guardians of the Rift]] provides 5,000–6,000 Crafting experience per hour at no cost.
* Crafting and alching jewellery from [[Gold bar|gold bars]] gives relatively slow but profitable experience.

==Glassblowing: 35-99==
One of the most common and reliable ways of training Crafting is to blow [[molten glass]]. There are multiple ways to acquire the resources needed to do so based on your account's progression.

=== 35-61: Buying buckets of sand and soda ash ===
Early on, the easiest way to acquire [[Bucket of sand|buckets of sand]] and [[soda ash]] is to buy the supplies from [[Trader Crewmember|trader crewmembers]]. Smelt the soda ash and buckets of sand together in a furnace to create [[molten glass]]. Blow this glass into the highest tier item you can until 61 Crafting. After level 46, glass can be blown into [[Unpowered orb|unpowered orbs]] and later [[Charge Orb|charged]] and crafted into [[battlestaves]] for more experience and profit.

=== 61-99 Superglass Make ===

==== Farming giant seaweed and mining sand ====
After 61 Crafting, 77 Magic, and completion of [[Lunar Diplomacy]], it is much faster to use [[Superglass Make]] to process bulk quantities of sand and [[giant seaweed]] you acquire from the [[Bandit Camp Quarry]] and [[Underwater|Underwater farming]], respectively.

Compared to buying soda ash and regular seaweed, the benefits include:
* [[Seaweed spores]] spawn frequently on the ground near the seaweed patches, requiring very little investment into getting them.
* With [[ultra compost]], around 50 giant seaweed per run can be collected.  Contrary to popular belief, [[magic secateurs]] do not affect the yield.<ref>[[Magic secateurs#:~:text%3DNote%2C%20magic%20secateurs%20do%20not%2Cit%20is%20a%20Limpwurt%20plant.|Note, magic secateurs do '''not''' work when farming ]][[Giant seaweed]] in [[Seaweed patch|Seaweed patches]] nor harvesting from a [[Flower patch]] unless it is a [[Limpwurt plant]].</ref> [[Seaweed (Farming)|Seaweed plants]] also benefit substantially from [[Attas plant|Attas plants]], although they require 76 [[Farming]].
* Superglass make can be cast directly on the giant seaweed, cooking it into soda ash is not required.
* Superglass make gives roughly 60% bonus molten glass with giant seaweed, and processes the entire inventory in one cast.

[[File:Bandit Camp Quarry.png|thumb|The [[Bandit Camp Quarry]], home of [[Sandstone]]]]
The fastest way of getting [[Bucket of sand|buckets of sand]] is to mine sandstone in the [[Bandit Camp Quarry|Quarry]] and grind it using [[Sandstorm]] just west of the mine. Noted empty [[bucket]]s can be given to [[Drew]] at the grinder. Players can then claim noted [[buckets of sand]] from Drew after grinding sandstone, with each piece of sandstone ground providing a different amount of sand depending on the size of the piece. Drew charges 50 coins per bucket.

Players may also collect buckets of sand by casting teleport home to [[Yanille]] and filling buckets at the [[sand pit]] north of the Home Portal. Alternatively, upon completion of the quest Song of the Elves, players gain access to a sand pit in Prifddinas which is a few steps away from the north bank. These methods require less effort than mining sandstone, but are significantly slower.

Completing [[The Hand in the Sand]] quest allows the player to claim 84 free buckets of sand daily from [[Bert]].

Players can farm [[giant seaweed]] by planting [[seaweed spores]] in [[seaweed patch]]es in the underwater area of [[Fossil Island]]. Harvesting these seaweed patches grant a large amount of giant seaweed, one of which is equivalent to six normal seaweeds. For more info, see:[[Ironman Guide/Farming#Giant seaweed]].

Once supplies have been collected, players can withdraw 18 buckets of sand and three giant seaweeds before casting Superglass Make to create molten glass. Blow the molten glass into the highest-tier glass item available for Crafting experience. Alternatively, blow glass into unpowered orbs for additional Crafting experience and GP from battlestaves or [[Empty light orb|empty light orbs]] for additional Crafting and [[Firemaking]] xp at [[Dorgesh-Kaan]].

[[File:Trader Stan's Trading Post (Port Sarim).png|thumb|right|[[Trader Stan's Trading Post]]]]

==== Charter ship method ====
The charter ship method still offers high Crafting experience per hour and does not require any banked supplies. The downside is that there usually is some competition for stock.

Buy buckets of sand and seaweed (or soda ash) from any [[Trader Crewmember]], cast [[Superglass Make]] and make the highest-tier glass item available on the spot. Sell the glass items or drop them, hop worlds and repeat. This method will grant approximately 65,000–70,000 experience per hour with [[lantern lens]]es and 85,000–90,000 experience per hour with [[empty light orb]]s, depending on stock. 

For best results, use this method in ports that are less popular. Areas like [[Port Tyras]] (requires [[Regicide]]), [[Brimhaven]] dock, and [[Mos Le'Harmless]] have a better chance of being stocked. Popular ports such as [[Port Khazard]] or [[Catherby]] are more frequently sold out, resulting in far less experience per hour.

=== Level 87-99 Fixing goblin lamps in Dorgesh-Kaan ===
{{Map|2699,5256|2695,5260|2868,5392|2698,5269|2735,5278|2739,5253|2869,5411|2749,5261|2801,5337|2865,5426|2738,5283|2749,5292|2764,5370|2804,5351|2744,5299|2690,5302|2802,5359|2869,5422|2698,5302|2707,5274|2869,5415|2806,5348|2796,5337|2801,5343|2774,5335|2772,5343|2872,5410|2760,5359|2823,5422|2827,5417|2827,5433|2823,5429|2758,5396|2762,5409|2770,5419|2781,5429|2801,5428|2804,5427|2798,5415|2807,5400|2803,5389|2874,5483|2867,5490|2864,5491|2857,5496|2770,5413|2758,5398|2691,5328|2701,5345|2706,5354|2701,5362|2706,5369|2745,5360|2739,5360|2736,5350|2747,5348|2741,5344|2746,5323|2749,5329|2742,5327|2737,5324|2744,5348|2807,5406|2766,5431|mtype=dot|mapID=5|align=right|caption=Map of lamps in Dorgesh-Kaan}}Fixing [[Lamp (Dorgesh-Kaan)|lamps]] in [[Dorgesh-Kaan]] is the way to get the most experience out of each [[molten glass]]. It requires 87 [[Crafting]], 44 Thieving, 52 Firemaking, and completion of [[The Lost Tribe]]. 

Molten glass is used to craft [[Light orb|light orbs]], which then repair lamps in Dorgesh-Kaan that give on average 724 Crafting experience, 550 [[Firemaking]] experience, and small amounts of Thieving experience.  

Players should take a [[glassblowing pipe]] along with an inventory of molten glass out of the nearby bank and run to the [[wire machine]]. On the way, glassblow [[Empty light orb|empty light orbs]]. Once there, thieve [[cave goblin wire]] from the wire machine and attach it to the empty light orbs. Upon crafting the completed light orbs, work your way around the city fixing the lamps.  

==== Fixing the lamps ====
Around ten lamps will be broken at any one time, and are unique to each player; each player will see different lamps around Dorgesh-Kaan as broken. Upon fixing a lamp, should the player still be carrying additional light orbs afterwards, they will be notified whether there is another lamp in need of fixing nearby. This will be accompanied by a flashing arrow on their minimap if so. The player should bring low-weight equipment such as the [[Graceful outfit]]. They may wish to bring [[Stamina potion|stamina potions]] and the [[ring of endurance]] to help with energy management. 

Tip: [[Dorgesh-kaan sphere]] can be used to teleport randomly around Dorgesh-Kaan if a player is not near any broken lamps. These can be thieved from the chests, noted below, or bought from [[Oldak]] for 2 [[Law rune|law runes]] and 1 molten glass. 

==== Experience rates ====
Creating an empty light orb gives the player 70 experience. Adding goblin wire to complete the light orb grants another 104 experience.

For fixing a lamp, the player receives 500 Firemaking and 500 Crafting experience.

Every fifty lamps the player fixes, an additional 2,500 experience will be granted to both Crafting and Firemaking. 

Skilled players can reach 130,000 Crafting experience, 90,000 Firemaking experience, and 4000 Thieving experience per hour.

While still learning, players should expect as low as 90,000 Crafting and 65,000 Firemaking and 3000 Thieving experience per hour.

If while fixing the lamps, the player also thieves the nearby chests at 78+ Thieving, a skilled player can expect more than 95,000 Crafting experience per hour, 70,000 Firemaking experience per hour, and 75,000 Thieving experience per hour. It takes some practice to get a good rhythmn and balance between the three but if a good route is used the player can expect decent experience in all three skills.

==== Extra note: Chests in Dorgesh-Kaan ====
Players with 78 Thieving can thieve from the [[Chest (Dorgesh-Kaan Average)|average chest]] and [[Chest (Dorgesh-Kaan Rich)|rich chest]], which are both found in high numbers near lamps. These can grant additional light orbs, however the odds of receiving them are relatively low. The chests grant 200 Thieving experience and 650 Thieving experience per successful attempt, respectively. This will mean the player gains less Crafting experience, but more Thieving experience.

Both chests can provide extra [[cave goblin wire]], and the rich chests provide [[Empty light orb|empty light orbs]] and [[Light orb|light orbs]]. This means that the player can restock some supplies as they go. 

The player should bring [[Lockpick|lockpicks]] if Thieving the chests.

== Other methods ==

===Crafting battlestaves===
Charging [[Unpowered orb|orbs]] and crafting [[Battlestaff|battlestaves]] offers relatively decent Crafting experience and very good profit.

Players who have completed task sets of the [[Varrock Diary]] can buy noted [[Battlestaff|battlestaves]] daily from a barrel near [[Zaff]] for 7,000 coins each. They all have to be bought at once, so a sizeable stack of coins is necessary. Starting at 15 with the easy tasks, each task set doubles the number of battlestaves that can be purchased per day. Players can also purchase a limited number of battlestaves from Zaff and various other vendors across Gielinor.

Players can also get battlestaves from various bosses and monsters, such as [[Zulrah]], [[Vorkath]], [[The Gauntlet]], [[Alchemical Hydra]] and [[Skeletal Wyvern]]s. [[Water orb|Water orbs]] can be obtained as a common drop from [[Moons of Peril]]. Each bought and crafted battlestaff is worth {{Coins|{{HA|Air battlestaff}}-7000}} profit when high alched.

Alternatively, players can buy battlestaves in bulk quantities (via world hopping) from magic shops such as [[Baba Yaga's Magic Shop.|Baba Yaga's Magic Shop]] at Lunar Isle (requiring completion of [[Lunar Diplomacy]]) or at the [[Magic Guild Store (Runes and Staves)|Magic Guild Store]] (requiring [[The Hand in the Sand]] and 66 Magic to access).

