[[File:TzHaar-Hur-Rin's Ore and Gem Store.png|thumb|right|[[TzHaar-Hur-Rin's Ore and Gem Store]] in [[Mor Ul Rek]]]]
===Cutting Gems===
There are a multitude of ways to acquire gems from skilling, shops, or passively through PVM. Cutting gems gives relatively fast XP when processed.

==== Buying Gems in Mor Ul Rek ====
This method becomes viable once the player has obtained a [[fire cape]] and accrued approximately {{Coins|3,200,000}}. Players can acquire Tokkul by selling chaos runes to [[TzHaar-Mej-Roh's Rune Store]], then use the Tokkul to purchase gems from [[TzHaar-Hur-Rin's Ore and Gem Store]].
* With a [[fire cape]] and enough capital, you can buy gems with chaos runes from [[TzHaar-Hur-Rin's Ore and Gem Store]]. Around 3,200,000 coins of capital is needed for the [[gold bars]], [[chaos rune]]s and [[nature rune]]s all at once, you can easily get away with just 1,000,000 coins if you do it in 3 sets. You will only end up losing around 18,000 chaos runes for 62 Crafting.

* If using chaos runes and [[Karamja gloves]] to earn [[Tokkul]] it is a 4:1 ratio for chaos runes to sapphires. This method can reliably earn around 40,000–50,000 Crafting experience per hour.

==== Gem rocks ====
[[Gem rocks|Mining gem rocks]], especially after completion of medium Karamja diary, gives competitive Mining XP rates while also banking a large quantity of gems to cut and turn into jewellery. It is also the most notable source of [[uncut opal]], [[Uncut jade|jade]], and [[Uncut red topaz|red topaz]]. Wearing a charged [[amulet of glory]] will increase mining speed significantly.

==== Shooting Stars ====
[[Stardust]] is obtained by mining the [[Crashed Star|Crashed star]]. Stardust is used as currency at [[Dusuri's Star Shop]] that can be used to purchase the [[Bag full of gems]] for 300 [[Stardust]]. This is a non intensive/afk training method that provides decent [[Mining]] experience alongside collecting gems.

Experience rates vary greatly based on level, the tier of pickaxe used, and time spent locating stars. If mining consistently, players can expect between 22,000 and 32,000 experience per hour, and 600–1000 stardust per hour. This equates to be around 80–120 gems per hour.

==== Rusty Chest ====
The [[Rusty chest|Rusty Chest]] on [[Dognose Island]] has a common chance of dropping [[gems]], allowing for a free method to train both [[Crafting]], and [[Thieving]]. The method requires 33 [[Thieving]] to open the chest, and 40 [[Sailing]] to reach the island. Should one wish to save the gems, bringing a [[gem bag]] will allow you to transport more gems per trip.

==== Port Roberts ====
Stalls in [[Port Roberts]] allow the player to obtain both uncut gems and silver ore/bars which can both be used for Crafting experience. This requires 75 [[Thieving]], and 50 [[Sailing]] to access Port Roberts for the first time.

==== Corrupted Gauntlet ====
Uncut gems are frequently rewarded from the [[The Gauntlet|Corrupted Gauntlet]], players will likely accrue a significant number of gems while hunting for their crystal equipment drops. The Gauntlet is located in [[Prifddinas]] which requires completion of [[Song of the Elves]] to access.

=== Jewellery ===
Making [[jewellery]] not only gives good Crafting experience, but it also provides valuable items to [[High Level Alchemy|alch]] for profit or sell to stores such as [[Grum's Gold Exchange]] or [[Davon's Amulet Store]]. They also provide useful teleport locations and item effects when [[Enchantment spells|enchanted]]. To make jewellery you must first obtain either [[Gold bar|gold bars]] or [[Silver bar|silver bars]]. It is recommended to also use [[gems]] in jewellery for more coins and Crafting experience. Gold bars can be used to make [[sapphire]], [[emerald]], [[ruby]], [[diamond]], [[dragonstone]], [[onyx]], and [[zenyte]] jewellery. Generally, [[Bracelet|bracelets]] provide the best alch profit while [[Amulet|amulets]] provide 5 experience more as well as 4 experience for stringing them at the cost of less alch profit.

[[Gold bar|Gold bars]] can also be used alone to make jewellery. It is recommended to either craft them into [[Gold bracelet|gold bracelets]] for alching or [[Gold tiara|gold tiaras]] for better experience. Players can use around 1,400 to 1,700 gold bars per hour from running to and from the [[Edgeville furnace]] or the closer [[Prifddinas#Trahaearn district|Prifddinas furnace]], resulting in 35,000 to 42,500 experience per hour if crafting bracelets or 49,000 to 59,500 experience per hour if crafting tiaras.

[[Silver bar|Silver bars]] can be used to make [[opal]], [[jade]], and [[red topaz]] jewellery. Getting lots of these gems nearly exclusively comes from mining [[gem rocks]]. See the money making guide [[Money making guide/Mining gemstones|mining gemstones]] for how to do this efficiently. When using silver bars alone, it is recommended to make either [[Tiara|tiaras]] for future [[Runecrafting]] experience or [[silver bolts (unf)]] for future [[Fletching]] experience.

===Obtaining Gold and Silver===

* [[Gold ore]] and [[silver ore]] can be bought from [[Ore seller]] in the [[Blast Furnace]], then smelted into bars.
* [[Zalcano]] is known for dropping smithing supplies which includes gold and silver ore as well as diamonds and dragonstones.
* [[Slayer monsters]] such as [[Gargoyle|gargoyles]] and [[Greater Nechryael|greater nechryaels]] can drop gold bars.
* [[Eclectic impling|Eclectic implings]] drop noted gold bars and their spawn locations can be camped in [[Puro-Puro]].
* Many [[Boss|Bosses]] drop noted gold ore such as [[Venenatis]], The [[Kalphite Queen]], [[Calvar'ion]], The [[Thermonuclear smoke devil]], [[Phantom Muspah]], [[Spindel]], [[The Nightmare]], [[Phosani's Nightmare]], [[Vet'ion]], [[King Black Dragon]], [[Grotesque Guardians]], and The [[Deranged archaeologist]].
* Silver bars can be obtained directly from [[Reward token|Temple Trekking rewards]].
* The [[Phantom Muspah]] and [[Crazy archaeologist]] both drop silver ore.
* The rewards [[Ancient chest|chest]] from [[Chambers of Xeric]] drops both gold and silver while [[Monumental chest|Theatre of Blood]] and [[Chest (Tombs of Amascut)|Tombs of Amascut]] only drop gold.
* [[Casket (Reward pool)]] from defeating [[Tempoross]] are also a decent source of gold and silver bars as well as gems.

=== Dragonhide equipment ===
A sizeable amount of dragonhides are obtained from killing [[green dragon]]s for [[Prayer]] experience and from killing [[Vorkath]]. Tan the hides in the [[Crafting Guild]] or by casting [[Tan Leather]], craft the leathers into dragonhide bodies and [[high alch]] them for money.

=== Drift Nets ===
[[Jute fibre]] can be farmed in hops patches and woven into [[Drift net|drift nets]] for 55 Crafting experience for every two jute fibres. This is a comparable amount of experience per item crafted to glassblowing. The drift nets can then be used to train Hunter and Fishing in [[drift net fishing]], in the same area as the Giant seaweed patches. The amount of Crafting experience banked per jute run varies depending on Farming level, whether you have the [[magic secateurs]], whether an [[Attas seed|attas]] seed is planted, what kind of [[Compost Bin|compost]] (or protection) is used, and luck, but at higher farming levels, somewhere between 1000 and 2000 Crafting experience worth of jute fibre per run is likely. A good place to weave drift nets is at the Fossil Island camp, where, once built, a bank chest and a loom are very close together (and [[planks]] can also be collected from the spawns while running between the two tents, if desired, for later construction training). This is a simpler, slower, cheaper, and more passive way to accumulate Crafting experience over a long time as compared with glassblowing, and can be easily combined with giant seaweed farming or other methods of training Crafting for more efficient training.

